  script: /usr/bin/security show-keychain-info '<dir>/user/Library/Keychains/login.keychain-db' >/dev/null 2>&1
  proof: fails
  control: /usr/bin/security show-keychain-info '<dir>/user/Library/Keychains/login.keychain-db' >/dev/null 2>&1
resources | have a hard limit above 256 open files
  script: v=$(ulimit -Hn); case "$v" in unlimited) exit 0 ;; ''|*[!0-9]*) echo "unreadable limit: $v"; exit 0 ;; esac; test "$v" -gt 256
  proof: fails
  control: v=$(ulimit -Hn); case "$v" in unlimited) exit 0 ;; ''|*[!0-9]*) echo "unreadable limit: $v"; exit 0 ;; esac; test "$v" -gt 256
keychain | read a keychain item
  script: /usr/bin/security find-generic-password -s 'enclos.abc.probe' -a 'home/probe' -w '<dir>/user/probe.keychain-db' 2>/dev/null
  proof: output lacks 656e636c6f732d70726f6265
  control: /usr/bin/security find-generic-password -s 'enclos.abc.probe' -a 'home/probe' -w '<dir>/user/probe.keychain-db' 2>/dev/null | /usr/bin/grep -q 656e636c6f732d70726f6265
pasteboard | read the pasteboard
  script: /usr/bin/pbpaste >/dev/null
  proof: fails
  control: /usr/bin/pbpaste >/dev/null
crontab | read the crontab
  script: /usr/bin/crontab -l >/dev/null
  proof: fails with /usr/bin/crontab: Operation not permitted
  control: /usr/bin/crontab -l >/dev/null
  closed by: seatbelt: Seatbelt itself refuses to run setuid programs, whatever the policy; no enclos rule is tested
at | list the `at` queue
  script: /usr/bin/atq >/dev/null
  proof: fails with /usr/bin/atq: Operation not permitted
  control: /usr/bin/atq >/dev/null
  closed by: seatbelt: Seatbelt itself refuses to run setuid programs, whatever the policy; no enclos rule is tested
### host services
launchservices | open a folder through LaunchServices
  script: /usr/bin/open -g /System
  proof: fails with Code=-10661
  control: /usr/bin/pgrep -x Finder >/dev/null
  closed by: baseline: on (deny default) the baseline refuses something the tool needs (likely a lookup; not traced) before the route's rule is reached; the rule itself is shown only by a run on (allow default), as enclos's CI makes
apple events | send an Apple Event to Finder
  script: /usr/bin/osascript -e 'with timeout of 8 seconds' -e 'tell application "Finder" to count windows' -e 'end timeout'
  proof: apple event blocked: application "Finder". (-1728)
  control: /usr/bin/pgrep -x Finder >/dev/null
  closed by: baseline: on (deny default) the baseline refuses something the tool needs (likely a lookup; not traced) before the route's rule is reached; the rule itself is shown only by a run on (allow default), as enclos's CI makes
launchd | submit a launchd job
  script: /bin/launchctl submit -l org.enclos.probe.7 -- /usr/bin/true
  proof: fails
  control: /bin/launchctl print gui/$(/usr/bin/id -u) >/dev/null 2>&1
  host: the launchd job org.enclos.probe.7
preferences | write preferences through cfprefsd
  script: /usr/bin/defaults write org.enclos.probe.7 probe -string written
  proof: fails
  control: /usr/bin/defaults domains >/dev/null 2>&1
  host: the preferences domain org.enclos.probe.7
launch agents | write in ~/Library/LaunchAgents
  script: echo x > '<dir>/user/Library/LaunchAgents/enclos-probe-7'
  proof: fails
  control: test -w '<dir>/user/Library/LaunchAgents'
  host: the file <dir>/user/Library/LaunchAgents/enclos-probe-7
